:\".youtube.com\";s:13:\"duration_days\";i:180;s:8:\"category\";s:9:\"marketing\";s:8:\"provider\";s:16:\"YouTube (Google)\";s:7:\"purpose\";s:65:\"Stores the visitor\'s cookie consent state for the current domain.\";s:11:\"description\";s:64:\"Set by YouTube to record the visitor\'s privacy/consent metadata.\";}i:3;a:7:{s:4:\"name\";s:4:\"PREF\";s:6:\"domain\";s:12:\".youtube.com\";s:13:\"duration_days\";i:240;s:8:\"category\";s:10:\"functional\";s:8:\"provider\";s:16:\"YouTube (Google)\";s:7:\"purpose\";s:62:\"Stores player preferences such as preferred playback settings.\";s:11:\"description\";s:55:\"Set by YouTube to remember embedded-player preferences.\";}i:4;a:7:{s:4:\"name\";s:7:\"CONSENT\";s:6:\"domain\";s:11:\".google.com\";s:13:\"duration_days\";i:730;s:8:\"category\";s:10:\"functional\";s:8:\"provider\";s:6:\"Google\";s:7:\"purpose\";s:55:\"Stores the visitor\'s consent state for Google services.\";s:11:\"description\";s:55:\"Set by Google to persist the visitor\'s consent choices.\";}}}s:7:\"zendesk\";a:7:{s:5:\"label\";s:7:\"Zendesk\";s:11:\"description\";s:31:\"Customer support and live chat.\";s:8:\"category\";s:10:\"functional\";s:3:\"pro\";b:1;s:14:\"gcm_compatible\";b:0;s:8:\"patterns\";a:4:{s:7:\"scripts\";a:2:{i:0;s:19:\"static.zdassets.com\";i:1;s:16:\"ekr.zdassets.com\";}s:7:\"iframes\";a:0:{}s:6:\"styles\";a:0:{}s:5:\"media\";a:0:{}}s:7:\"cookies\";a:0:{}}s:23:\"iubenda-legal-documents\";a:7:{s:5:\"label\";s:23:\"iubenda Legal Documents\";s:11:\"description\";s:130:\"Displays iubenda-hosted privacy policy, cookie policy and terms. Sets no cookies. Does not cover iubenda\'s Cookie Solution banner.\";s:8:\"category\";s:9:\"essential\";s:3:\"pro\";b:1;s:14:\"gcm_compatible\";b:0;s:8:\"patterns\";a:4:{s:7:\"scripts\";a:6:{i:0;s:26:\"cdn.iubenda.com/iubenda.js\";i:1;s:33:\"cdn.iubenda.com/iubenda_badge.css\";i:2;s:31:\"www.iubenda.com/privacy-policy/\";i:3;s:37:\"www.iubenda.com/terms-and-conditions/\";i:4;s:39:\"www.iubenda.com/assets/builds/legaldocs\";i:5;s:41:\"www.iubenda.com/assets/privacy_policy.css\";}s:7:\"iframes\";a:0:{}s:6:\"styles\";a:2:{i:0;s:33:\"cdn.iubenda.com/iubenda_badge.css\";i:1;s:41:\"www.iubenda.com/assets/privacy_policy.css\";}s:5:\"media\";a:0:{}}s:7:\"cookies\";a:0:{}}s:12:\"powerfuldocs\";a:7:{s:5:\"label\";s:13:\"Powerful Docs\";s:11:\"description\";s:33:\"Documentation and support widget.\";s:8:\"category\";s:10:\"functional\";s:3:\"pro\";b:1;s:14:\"gcm_compatible\";b:0;s:8:\"patterns\";a:4:{s:7:\"scripts\";a:1:{i:0;s:20:\"app.powerfuldocs.com\";}s:7:\"iframes\";a:0:{}s:6:\"styles\";a:0:{}s:5:\"media\";a:0:{}}s:7:\"cookies\";a:0:{}}s:15:\"subscribers-com\";a:7:{s:5:\"label\";s:15:\"Subscribers.com\";s:11:\"description\";s:2143:\"Web push notification service (subscribers.com). Loads an opt-in prompt and registers a push service worker. PATTERN: host-level `cdn.subscribers.com` covers both shipped scripts, `/assets/subscribers.js` (the documented embed) and `/assets/subscribers-sw.js` (the service worker). The host is a dedicated single-vendor CDN with no third-party content on it, so a host pattern carries no over-blocking risk and matches how OneSignal (`cdn.onesignal.com`) and PushEngage (`clientcdn.pushengage.com`) are already catalogued. DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED: `app.subscribers.com/api/v1/`, `hi.subscribers.com` (telemetry beacon) and `apn.subscribers.com/apn` (Safari legacy push). These are fetch/XHR/beacon endpoints called from the bundle, not script or iframe sources, so a script pattern would never match them and adding them would be misleading. COOKIE: one only, `isPushNotificationClient`, which suppresses the opt-in prompt after a visitor dismisses it. Duration is publisher-configurable: 7 days by default, and the \"never show again\" sentinel is rewritten to 3650 days. Confirmed by reading the live minified bundle; `document.cookie` is touched in exactly two places. Note `__cfduid` appears against this host in Cookiepedia but is a stale Cloudflare cookie, not a vendor cookie, and should not be attributed here. CATEGORY NOTE FOR REVIEW: filed as `functional` to stay consistent with OneSignal and PushEngage, which are direct competitors already published as `functional`, and because the single cookie is a prompt-suppression preference rather than a tracking identifier. An argument exists for `marketing`, since the product\'s purpose is promotional re-engagement and DuckDuckGo Tracker Radar scores it fingerprinting: 2. Worth a deliberate decision at approval: if `marketing` is preferred, OneSignal and PushEngage should move with it rather than leaving three near-identical services split across two categories. SOURCE: found leaking pre-consent on a customer site in ticket 1521922. Absent from Open Cookie Database, Cookiepedia and other public cookie databases; EasyPrivacy carries only the broad `||subscribers.com^$third-party`.\";s:8:\"category\";s:9:\"marketing\";s:3:\"pro\";b:1;s:14:\"gcm_compatible\";b:0;s:8:\"patterns\";a:4:{s:7:\"scripts\";a:1:{i:0;s:19:\"cdn.subscribers.com\";}s:7:\"iframes\";a:0:{}s:6:\"styles\";a:0:{}s:5:\"media\";a:0:{}}s:7:\"cookies\";a:1:{i:0;a:7:{s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"isPushNotificationClient\";s:6:\"domain\";s:30:\"first-partypublishersowndomain\";s:13:\"duration_days\";i:3650;s:8:\"category\";s:10:\"functional\";s:8:\"provider\";s:15:\"Subscribers.com\";s:7:\"purpose\";s:107:\"Remembers that the visitor dismissed the web push opt-in prompt, so it is not shown again until it expires.\";s:11:\"description\";s:582:\"Written first-party by the vendor\'s JavaScript via document.cookie with path=/, not set by subscribers.com as a third-party cookie. Observed value is the literal string \"false\". Duration is publisher-configurable: the bundle\'s own default is 7 days, and the \"never show again\" sentinel (-1) is rewritten to 3650 days, which is the figure recorded here so the disclosure covers the worst case rather than understating retention. Categorised as preferences because the cookie itself only suppresse